没错，要有耐心去演绎那种克制。

901
00:44:26.360 --> 00:44:26.700
Yes.
是的。

902
00:44:26.900 --> 00:44:31.020
And to not try to overload the scene with their own bits.
而且不会试图用自己的即兴发挥来喧宾夺主。

903
00:44:31.360 --> 00:44:31.740
Yeah.
没错。

904
00:44:32.120 --> 00:44:33.380
And she does it perfectly.
她做得非常完美。

905
00:44:33.680 --> 00:44:38.040
Incidentally, she graduated from the University of Missouri's theater program.
顺便说一下，她毕业于密苏里大学的戏剧专业。

906
00:44:38.380 --> 00:44:39.640
Good old Mizzou.
老牌密苏里大学。

907
00:44:39.860 --> 00:44:43.760
That was about 90 minutes away from the school that I went to in Kirksville, Missouri.
那离我上学的密苏里州柯克斯维尔大约有90分钟的路程。

908
00:44:43.760 --> 00:44:48.520
I had to drive through Mizzou, Columbia, Missouri, to get to Kirksville.
我得穿过密苏里州哥伦比亚市的密苏里大学才能到达柯克斯维尔。

909
00:44:48.760 --> 00:44:50.480
You and Brooke crisscrossing.
你和布鲁克在那儿交错而过。

910
00:44:50.860 --> 00:44:51.280
Exactly.
没错。

911
00:44:51.460 --> 00:44:52.200
I know.
我知道。

912
00:44:52.340 --> 00:44:56.200
We're both two gals from theater schools in Missouri who landed on the office.
我们俩都是来自密苏里州戏剧学校的女孩，最后都来到了《办公室》剧组。

913
00:44:56.420 --> 00:44:56.840
Go Mo.
密苏里加油。

914
00:44:57.240 --> 00:45:00.960
The scene between Margaret and Michael is so cringy.
玛格丽特和迈克尔之间的那场戏真是尴尬得让人脚趾扣地。

915
00:45:01.280 --> 00:45:04.960
Michael literally is like rubbing his forehead like he's in pain.
迈克尔简直就像是在揉着额头，好像很痛苦一样。

916
00:45:05.300 --> 00:45:09.420
He's like, so you get the rent checks every month?
他说，所以你每个月都能收到房租支票？

917
00:45:09.660 --> 00:45:10.780
And she's like, yeah.
她说，是的。

918
00:45:11.440 --> 00:45:12.240
I mean, it's like.
我是说，这简直了。

919
00:45:12.340 --> 00:45:12.640
I know.
我知道。

920
00:45:12.640 --> 00:45:14.500
He's like, and then what do you do with them?
他说，那你收到之后都怎么处理呢？

921
00:45:14.700 --> 00:45:18.920
And she goes, are you really asking me what I do with the checks that people give me?
她说，你真的在问我怎么处理别人给我的支票吗？

922
00:45:19.180 --> 00:45:21.620
And he's like, I'm just I'm trying to make conversation, OK?
他说，我只是……我只是想找点话题聊聊，行吗？

923
00:45:22.220 --> 00:45:22.960
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

924
00:45:23.240 --> 00:45:27.080
And he just talks about like, he goes, well, this is who I was dating before you.
然后他开始谈论，他说，好吧，这是我在和你交往之前约会过的人。

925
00:45:27.320 --> 00:45:29.280
And he shows the photo of Jan.
接着他展示了简的照片。

926
00:45:29.800 --> 00:45:31.880
And then he calls her by accident.
然后他不小心拨通了她的电话。

927
00:45:31.880 --> 00:45:33.860
It's just like layer of layer of cringy.
这简直是一层又一层的尴尬。

928
00:45:33.980 --> 00:45:39.100
And then he kind of starts opening up to Margaret about like how it's so hard to find someone.
然后他开始向玛格丽特敞开心扉，说找个人有多难。

929
00:45:39.300 --> 00:45:40.920
And he tells her, you know, thanks.
他告诉她，你知道，谢谢你。

930
00:45:41.140 --> 00:45:41.900
This has been nice.
这感觉真不错。

931
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:44.280
Talking to the old lady on the bus.
和公交车上的老太太聊天。

932
00:45:44.700 --> 00:45:45.360
Mm hmm.
嗯哼。

933
00:45:45.680 --> 00:45:46.900
And Margaret's had it.
玛格丽特受够了。

934
00:45:47.140 --> 00:45:48.160
She's like, you're rude.
她说，你真没礼貌。

935
00:45:48.360 --> 00:45:48.920
That was rude.
那太粗鲁了。

936
00:45:49.240 --> 00:45:51.480
Well, and then Michael says, well, now you've ruined it.
好吧，然后迈克尔说，好吧，现在你把它搞砸了。

937
00:45:51.900 --> 00:45:53.780
Michael was such a jerk in this scene.
迈克尔在这场戏里真是个混蛋。

938
00:45:54.140 --> 00:46:00.500
Listen, if you had any sympathy for him after dinner party, it evaporated after this scene.
听着，如果你在看完《晚宴》后对他还有一丝同情，那在这场戏之后也烟消云散了。

939
00:46:00.860 --> 00:46:01.100
Yeah.
没错。

940
00:46:01.100 --> 00:46:08.200
We were very good at taking you on quite the roller coaster as your feelings for Michael are concerned on this show.
在让观众对迈克尔的感情产生过山车般的起伏方面，我们确实很擅长。

941
00:46:08.380 --> 00:46:10.780
But at this scene, I was like, you deserve Jan.
但在这一幕，我心想，你活该和简在一起。

942
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:13.260
You deserve to sleep on the bench at the foot of the bed.
你活该睡在床尾的长凳上。

943
00:46:13.360 --> 00:46:14.460
You're being such a turd.
你真是个混蛋。

944
00:46:14.760 --> 00:46:15.200
Exactly.
没错。

945
00:46:15.200 --> 00:46:16.520
It's very complicated.
这非常复杂。

946
00:46:16.840 --> 00:46:24.720
Well, now we go into this wonderful scene where Andy and Kevin are going to meet with the heads of the five families.
好吧，现在我们进入了安迪和凯文去见五大家族负责人的精彩场景。

947
00:46:24.940 --> 00:46:25.140
Yeah.
没错。

948
00:46:25.440 --> 00:46:26.240
Make their plea.
去进行他们的恳求。

949
00:46:26.240 --> 00:46:30.860
They're in what looks like to be some kind of conference room at the Scranton Business Park.
他们身处的地方看起来像是斯克兰顿商业园里的某个会议室。

950
00:46:31.080 --> 00:46:38.300
I wanted to point out at 14 minutes, 12 seconds, how nice the freaking TV is in this conference room.
我想指出在14分12秒的时候，这个会议室里的电视机看起来有多棒。

951
00:46:38.540 --> 00:46:38.820
Yeah.
是啊。

952
00:46:38.820 --> 00:46:44.340
It is a true big flat screen TV, not like Michael's tiny one.
那真的是一台大平板电视，不像迈克尔那台小得可怜。

953
00:46:44.580 --> 00:46:52.200
Nothing like our crazy old tube TV that we roll in on a cart for our conference room scenes.
跟我们会议室里那种还得用推车推来推去的笨重老式显像管电视完全没法比。

954
00:46:52.420 --> 00:46:52.680
Yeah.
没错。

955
00:46:52.780 --> 00:46:54.960
It's like a fancy big flat screen TV.
就像那种高级的大平板电视。

956
00:46:55.580 --> 00:46:56.000
Yeah.
是啊。

957
00:46:56.600 --> 00:46:58.260
Imagine if Michael had seen it.
想象一下要是迈克尔看到了会怎样。

958
00:46:58.340 --> 00:46:59.280
He would have passed out.
他肯定会当场晕过去。

959
00:46:59.460 --> 00:47:04.380
Well, we asked Paul about shooting this scene, and I loved what he had to say.
我们问了保罗关于拍摄这场戏的感受，我很喜欢他的回答。

960
00:47:04.580 --> 00:47:05.320
Here it is.
就是这段。

961
00:47:05.880 --> 00:47:10.000
So, being on set, and sort of be careful what you wish for, because I'm a huge fan of the show.
当时在片场，真是应了那句“小心你许下的愿望”，因为我本身就是这部剧的超级粉丝。

962
00:47:10.160 --> 00:47:11.120
I think they're super funny.
我觉得他们真的超级搞笑。

963
00:47:11.260 --> 00:47:16.560
And I remember the first time we're about to shoot, they say, okay, quiet on the set.
我记得第一次准备开拍时，他们喊道：好了，片场安静。

964
00:47:17.160 --> 00:47:17.960
Camera's rolling.
摄像机开始转动了。

965
00:47:18.240 --> 00:47:19.680
And I will never forget it.
我永远忘不了那一刻。

966
00:47:19.740 --> 00:47:26.900
But Brian says, okay, nobody F off looks at me.
布莱恩突然说：好了，谁都不许看我。

967
00:47:27.300 --> 00:47:30.620
And, you know, he was messing around, but it was so funny.
你知道，他是在开玩笑，但真的太搞笑了。

968
00:47:30.780 --> 00:47:36.440
And then the entire time we shot the scene, I had my lines to say, but we shot it about 20, 30 times.
在拍摄整场戏的过程中，我虽然有台词要说，但我们拍了大概二三十遍。

969
00:47:36.960 --> 00:47:40.620
And every single time, Brian and Ed said different things.
每一次，布莱恩和艾德说的内容都不一样。

970
00:47:40.620 --> 00:47:42.580
And I happen to think they're super funny.
我恰好觉得他们特别逗。

971
00:47:42.760 --> 00:47:44.940
And it was very hard to keep a straight face.
要忍住不笑真的太难了。

972
00:47:45.120 --> 00:47:47.160
I never knew what was going to come out of their mouths.
我根本不知道他们下一句会蹦出什么话来。

973
00:47:47.380 --> 00:47:49.940
They were making faces at me, trying to get me to laugh.
他们对着我做鬼脸，想逗我笑。

974
00:47:50.180 --> 00:47:51.940
And I had to sit there and be dead serious.
而我必须坐在那儿，一脸严肃。

975
00:47:52.060 --> 00:47:53.900
I didn't want to be the guy to mess up the scene.
我可不想成为那个搞砸拍摄的人。

976
00:47:53.900 --> 00:47:59.440
And so working with people who were literally comic geniuses in their delivery and their timing,
所以，能和这些在台词表达和节奏把控上简直是喜剧天才的人合作，

977
00:47:59.440 --> 00:48:05.440
having to sit there and being the new guy on set and trying to keep a straight face and not to mess up was a challenge.
作为一个片场新人，坐在那儿努力保持严肃不笑场，确实是个挑战。

978
00:48:05.440 --> 00:48:10.740
But such a life, a life experience and just so funny to do.
但这真是一次人生体验，而且过程太有趣了。

979
00:48:10.860 --> 00:48:13.780
And I'm so honored to be a part of a small little part of the office.
能参与《办公室》的一小部分，我感到非常荣幸。

980
00:48:14.620 --> 00:48:16.860
I love that Brian and Ed were trying to mess with them.
我喜欢布莱恩和艾德试图捉弄他们这一点。

981
00:48:16.980 --> 00:48:17.800
We would do this.
我们确实会这样做。

982
00:48:17.800 --> 00:48:21.160
We would know when someone was going to break and we would have a little fun.
我们会观察谁快要破功了，然后找点乐子。

983
00:48:21.300 --> 00:48:21.940
We would.
我们确实会。

984
00:48:22.160 --> 00:48:22.540
It's true.
这是真的。

985
00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:26.720
Well, Paul mentioned to us, you know, what it was like to get lines at the last minute.
保罗跟我们提过，临时拿到台词是什么感觉。

986
00:48:26.760 --> 00:48:31.440
But he also talks to us about what it was like just being on the set and the lingo that they used.
他还跟我们聊了在片场的感觉，以及他们使用的那些行话。

987
00:48:31.980 --> 00:48:34.640
So we're shooting the scene over and over again.
当时我们一遍又一遍地拍那场戏。

988
00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:35.700
You know, we want to get it right.
你知道，我们想把它拍好。

989
00:48:35.860 --> 00:48:38.620
And sometimes the lines don't work, but the facial expressions are great.
有时候台词效果不好，但表情却很到位。

990
00:48:38.880 --> 00:48:43.460
So one of the guys comes in and says, when this happens, I forget the word he used.
所以其中一个人走过来，说了句什么，我忘了那个词是什么了。

991
00:48:43.560 --> 00:48:44.420
I want you to do this.
他说：我要你这样做。

992
00:48:44.580 --> 00:48:49.120
And then he walked out and I'm looking around like, I have no idea what that means.
然后他就走开了，我环顾四周，心想：我完全不知道那是什么意思。

993
00:48:49.360 --> 00:48:52.880
So the camera guy behind me, he's like, you don't know what that means?
我身后的摄像师就问：你不知道那是什么意思？

994
00:48:52.980 --> 00:48:54.900
I'm like, no, I've never done this before.
我说：不知道，我以前从没干过这个。

995
00:48:55.080 --> 00:48:58.960
He goes, OK, I'll tap you on the shoulder when you should say your line.
他说：好吧，该你说台词的时候，我会拍拍你的肩膀。

996
00:48:58.960 --> 00:49:01.540
So I was literally sitting there and something was going on.
所以我当时就坐在那儿，现场正进行着拍摄。

997
00:49:01.680 --> 00:49:05.560
And I felt the camera guy who was shooting over my shoulder tap me on the shoulder when
然后我感觉到在我身后拍摄的摄像师拍了拍我的肩膀，提示我

998
00:49:05.560 --> 00:49:06.320
to say my line.
该说台词了。

999
00:49:06.580 --> 00:49:10.300
And it was just sort of indicative of the whole experience because everybody was so friendly
这简直就是整个拍摄经历的缩影，因为每个人都非常友好，

1000
00:49:10.300 --> 00:49:12.540
and helpful and just wanted to get it done right.
乐于助人，而且只想把事情做好。

1001
00:49:13.420 --> 00:49:17.520
Except, I think, Brian and Ed, who were just trying to make me laugh the whole time.
除了布莱恩和埃德，我觉得他们当时只是想逗我笑。

1002
00:49:18.200 --> 00:49:22.360
Can I say, Angela, that when we got these audio clips from Paul, the thing that was
安吉拉，我能说吗，当我们收到保罗发来的这些音频片段时，最让我觉得

1003
00:49:22.360 --> 00:49:31.840
so fun for me was his observations as a non-actor being on a set, because it really took me back
有趣的是他作为一个非演员在片场的观察，因为它真的把我带回了

1004
00:49:31.840 --> 00:49:37.660
to all of those moments in my career as an actor where you just are learning on the fly.
我职业生涯中作为演员的所有那些时刻，你只能在实践中边做边学。

1005
00:49:37.780 --> 00:49:40.560
I didn't learn any of this stuff in theater school.
我在戏剧学校里可没学过这些东西。

1006
00:49:41.040 --> 00:49:43.980
And I don't even know if there is any other way to learn it.
而且我甚至不知道还有没有其他方法能学到这些。

1007
00:49:44.080 --> 00:49:45.600
You just kind of absorb it in the moment.
你只能在当下那种情境里去吸收它。

1008
00:49:45.600 --> 00:49:48.720
But he sent in an audio clip that is my favorite.
但他发来的一个音频片段是我的最爱。

1009
00:49:48.980 --> 00:49:49.560
Me too.
我也是。

1010
00:49:49.560 --> 00:49:51.940
Because I struggled with this too.
因为我也曾为此苦恼过。

1011
00:49:52.900 --> 00:49:56.380
You and I have talked about this, but I don't think we've ever talked about it on the pod.
你和我聊过这个，但我觉得我们从没在播客里聊过。

1012
00:49:56.540 --> 00:49:57.260
So this is great.
所以这太棒了。

1013
00:49:57.480 --> 00:50:00.480
I love that he had the same observation.
我很高兴他也有同样的观察。

1014
00:50:01.220 --> 00:50:03.180
Okay, we'll play it and then we'll talk about it.
好了，我们来播放一下，然后再聊聊它。

1015
00:50:03.480 --> 00:50:05.040
So this was a new experience for me.
这对我是全新的体验。

1016
00:50:05.180 --> 00:50:07.500
I kind of, it was my first time being really on the set.
我当时，那是我第一次真正待在片场。

1017
00:50:07.760 --> 00:50:10.480
And I'm sitting in my trailer going, well, what do I do now?
我坐在拖车里心想，好吧，现在我该干什么？

1018
00:50:10.580 --> 00:50:11.700
So I decided to get something to eat.
于是我决定去弄点吃的。

1019
00:50:12.020 --> 00:50:14.520
I walk out and I'm like, where can I get some food?
我走出来，心想，去哪儿能弄点吃的？

1020
00:50:14.560 --> 00:50:16.860
And they pointed me in the direction of where the breakfast was.
他们给我指了早餐的方向。

1021
00:50:16.860 --> 00:50:21.500
And as I started walking, I heard someone in the headset go, cool guy, Paul's going to breakfaSt.
当我开始走的时候，我听到有人在耳机里说，酷哥，保罗要去吃早餐了。

1022
00:50:21.960 --> 00:50:24.860
And then I come back and I hear them go, cool guy, Paul's back in his trailer.
然后我回来时，又听到他们说，酷哥，保罗回到拖车了。

1023
00:50:25.360 --> 00:50:27.660
Everywhere I went, someone's like, cool guy, Paul's in the bathroom.
我走到哪儿，都有人说，酷哥，保罗去洗手间了。

1024
00:50:28.180 --> 00:50:29.040
Cool guy, Paul's in it.
酷哥，保罗进去了。

1025
00:50:29.240 --> 00:50:31.060
Like someone had to know where I was at all times.
就好像有人必须时刻知道我在哪儿一样。

1026
00:50:31.160 --> 00:50:31.860
I thought it was really funny.
我觉得这真的很有趣。

1027
00:50:31.980 --> 00:50:35.100
They had to track me to make sure they knew where I was in case they needed me.
他们必须追踪我，以确保在需要我的时候能找到我。

1028
00:50:35.360 --> 00:50:38.740
So that was one super funny story from being on the set.
所以这是在片场发生的一个超级有趣的故事。

1029
00:50:38.740 --> 00:50:47.380
Yeah, you guys, on film and television sets, there is a whole network of production assistants
没错，伙计们，在电影和电视片场，有一整套制作助理网络，

1030
00:50:47.380 --> 00:50:52.380
that wear these walkie-talkies and they have little earpieces, kind of like the Secret Service,
他们戴着对讲机，还有小耳机，有点像特勤局，

1031
00:50:52.640 --> 00:50:53.140
you know?
你知道吗？

1032
00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:54.660
But not as fancy.
但没那么高级。

1033
00:50:54.920 --> 00:50:55.880
But not as fancy.
但没那么高级。

1034
00:50:56.040 --> 00:50:58.300
Like when they talk into them, you hear it echo.
就像他们对着对讲机说话时，你能听到回声。

1035
00:51:00.380 --> 00:51:04.980
Well, their job is literally to keep track of all the actors at all times.
嗯，他们的工作确实就是时刻追踪所有演员的动向。

1036
00:51:05.360 --> 00:51:09.920
And you can hear them tracking you all day as you walk by.
当你走过时，你能整天听到他们追踪你的声音。

1037
00:51:10.180 --> 00:51:11.180
As you walk by.
当你走过时。

1038
00:51:11.320 --> 00:51:15.780
And sometimes you hear it from the person directly behind you who's actually speaking about you.
有时你会直接从身后那个正在谈论你的人那里听到。

1039
00:51:15.920 --> 00:51:21.220
And then you hear it in stereo from the other person they're talking to as you walk past them.
然后当你走过他们身边时，又能从他们正在通话的另一个人那里听到立体声的回响。

1040
00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:25.340
And I guess the theory behind it, Jenna, is that production needs to know where we are
我想背后的理论是，珍娜，制作组需要知道我们在哪儿，

1041
00:51:25.340 --> 00:51:29.480
because if the scene is lit and ready, they need us on that soundstage ready to go.
因为如果场景灯光布置好了，他们需要我们立刻出现在摄影棚准备开拍。

1042
00:51:29.640 --> 00:51:34.480
And they can't have an actor unaccounted for because then that holds everyone up and it costs money, right?
他们不能让演员下落不明，因为那样会耽误所有人，而且很费钱，对吧？

1043
00:51:34.780 --> 00:51:35.040
Yeah.
没错。

1044
00:51:35.160 --> 00:51:37.860
So when they're lighting a scene, they let you go back to your trailer.
所以当他们在布置灯光时，会让你回拖车。

1045
00:51:38.220 --> 00:51:39.240
You might use the restroom.
你可能会去洗手间。

1046
00:51:39.340 --> 00:51:40.200
You might get a snack.
你可能会去吃点零食。

1047
00:51:40.360 --> 00:51:44.040
In our case, maybe we pop over to the writer's building and we're hanging out.
就我们而言，可能就是溜达到编剧大楼去闲逛。

1048
00:51:44.340 --> 00:51:47.920
But once the scene is ready, they have no time to lose.
但一旦场景准备好了，他们就一刻也不能耽误。

1049
00:51:48.380 --> 00:51:52.100
Because a production day is very regimented.
因为拍摄的一天是非常严格的。

1050
00:51:52.100 --> 00:51:55.660
And if you run out of time, that means you probably have to cut something.
如果时间不够了，那就意味着你可能得删减掉一些内容。

1051
00:51:56.120 --> 00:51:57.880
And you don't want that, right?
你肯定不想那样，对吧？

1052
00:51:58.020 --> 00:51:59.740
You don't want to have to cut content.
你不想不得不删减内容。

1053
00:52:00.180 --> 00:52:00.340
Right.
没错。

1054
00:52:00.520 --> 00:52:02.720
So, yeah, all day long.
所以，是的，整天都是这样。

1055
00:52:02.980 --> 00:52:08.280
But my favorite thing, Angela, is that they came up with a code for the bathroom.
但我最喜欢的一点是，安吉拉，他们竟然给上厕所设了个代号。

1056
00:52:08.280 --> 00:52:11.900
I guess maybe it's to be, I don't know, more discreet.
我想也许是为了，我不知道，更谨慎一点吧。

1057
00:52:12.100 --> 00:52:14.240
But everyone knows what the code is.
但每个人都知道那个代号是什么。

1058
00:52:14.340 --> 00:52:16.080
The code is 10-1.
代号是10-1。

1059
00:52:16.780 --> 00:52:17.780
Jenna is 10-1.
珍娜是10-1。

1060
00:52:17.780 --> 00:52:20.980
Everyone knows when you go to the bathroom on a set.
每个人都知道你什么时候在片场去上厕所。

1061
00:52:21.700 --> 00:52:23.160
Every single person.
每一个人。

1062
00:52:23.160 --> 00:52:25.880
It goes through every walkie-talkie.
它会通过每一个对讲机广播出来。

1063
00:52:26.400 --> 00:52:27.260
Angela 10-1.
安吉拉10-1。

1064
00:52:27.540 --> 00:52:28.220
Jenna 10-1.
珍娜10-1。

1065
00:52:28.740 --> 00:52:31.940
And I just want you to know, what if you need to 10-2?
我只想让你知道，如果你需要10-2怎么办？

1066
00:52:32.920 --> 00:52:34.660
And you're going to be in there for a minute.
而且你得在里面待上一会儿。

1067
00:52:34.980 --> 00:52:40.900
Every time they would announce Jenna is 10-1, I would get a lot of anxiety because I would
每次他们宣布珍娜10-1时，我都会感到非常焦虑，因为我会

1068
00:52:40.900 --> 00:52:43.620
think I better make it fast or they're going to think I'm doing a poop.
想我最好快点，否则他们会以为我在拉屎。

1069
00:52:44.040 --> 00:52:44.460
Right.
没错。

1070
00:52:44.460 --> 00:52:46.900
What about when we both started pumping?
那我们俩开始挤奶的时候呢？

1071
00:52:47.300 --> 00:52:49.680
And then you would hear in the walkie, Angela's pumping.
然后你就会在对讲机里听到，安吉拉在挤奶。

1072
00:52:50.060 --> 00:52:51.140
Angela's going to pump.
安吉拉要去挤奶了。

1073
00:52:51.540 --> 00:52:52.020
Yeah.
是的。

1074
00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:53.340
All your business.
你所有的私事。

1075
00:52:53.600 --> 00:52:56.100
All your business through a walkie-talkie.
你所有的私事都通过对讲机广播。

1076
00:52:56.300 --> 00:52:57.500
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1077
00:52:57.720 --> 00:53:00.500
And I get why they have to do it, but it is very surreal.
我明白他们为什么必须这样做，但这真的很超现实。

1078
00:53:00.740 --> 00:53:05.520
And so that clip from Paul really, Jenna and I immediately called each other.
所以保罗的那段录音，珍娜和我立刻就给对方打了电话。

1079
00:53:05.660 --> 00:53:06.420
We're like, oh my gosh.
我们当时想，天哪。

1080
00:53:06.820 --> 00:53:09.200
He talked about the thingy with the tracking.
他提到了那个追踪的小玩意儿。

1081
00:53:09.560 --> 00:53:10.080
The tracking.
那个追踪器。

1082
00:53:11.540 --> 00:53:14.120
They should warn you in film school.
他们在电影学院就应该警告你。

1083
00:53:14.380 --> 00:53:16.320
That you're going to be tracked all day.
你会整天被追踪。

1084
00:53:16.460 --> 00:53:19.100
They should warn you because it's very jarring at firSt.
他们应该警告你，因为起初这非常让人不安。

1085
00:53:19.360 --> 00:53:19.560
Yeah.
没错。

1086
00:53:20.060 --> 00:53:24.820
Well, let's just say that this meeting of the five families goes very well.
好吧，我们就说这次五大家族的会议进行得非常顺利。

1087
00:53:24.960 --> 00:53:26.700
It also goes very quickly.
而且进行得非常快。

1088
00:53:26.700 --> 00:53:28.620
In about three sentences, W.B.
大约三句话，W.B.

1089
00:53:28.740 --> 00:53:29.560
Jones agrees.
琼斯就同意了。

1090
00:53:30.100 --> 00:53:30.620
Fine.
好吧。

1091
00:53:30.620 --> 00:53:32.280
You can have your parking spaces back.
你们可以拿回你们的停车位了。

1092
00:53:32.420 --> 00:53:32.980
It's a triumph.
这简直是场胜利。

1093
00:53:33.320 --> 00:53:35.940
Listen, it looks like Kevin's about to cry.
听着，凯文看起来快要哭了。

1094
00:53:36.100 --> 00:53:37.800
And Bill Kress is not here for that.
而比尔·克雷斯可不想看这个。

1095
00:53:37.800 --> 00:53:41.020
He can't handle a grown man crying about a parking spot.
他受不了一个成年男人为了停车位哭泣。

1096
00:53:41.200 --> 00:53:42.820
And so Paul Faust calls it.
所以保罗·福斯特做了决定。

1097
00:53:42.940 --> 00:53:44.460
He's like, just give them their spots back.
他说，就把车位还给他们吧。

1098
00:53:44.600 --> 00:53:46.320
And it just wraps up so quickly.
事情就这样很快地结束了。

1099
00:53:46.520 --> 00:53:47.160
It does.
确实。

1100
00:53:47.320 --> 00:53:50.120
And then Paul has a great line where he says this could have been an email.
然后保罗有一句很棒的台词，他说这本来可以发封邮件解决的。

1101
00:53:50.460 --> 00:53:51.600
Which is like a meme.
这就像个梗一样。

1102
00:53:51.800 --> 00:53:53.100
It also speaks to me.
它也触动了我。

1103
00:53:53.500 --> 00:53:53.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1104
00:53:54.100 --> 00:53:57.620
I mean, Paul needs to get out and ride his motorcycle.
我是说，保罗得出去骑骑他的摩托车了。

1105
00:53:58.160 --> 00:53:58.860
He's done.
他受够了。

1106
00:54:00.340 --> 00:54:03.380
Kevin's talking head after this scene broke my heart.
这一幕之后凯文的采访片段让我心碎。

1107
00:54:03.800 --> 00:54:05.600
Brian did such a good job with it.
布莱恩演得太棒了。

1108
00:54:05.600 --> 00:54:10.300
He just says that after Stacey broke up with him, it was really a tough time.
他说在史黛西和他分手后，那段日子真的很难熬。

1109
00:54:10.560 --> 00:54:13.520
And, well, it's just nice to win one.
而且，能赢一次感觉真好。

1110
00:54:13.760 --> 00:54:15.100
And he tears up.
然后他热泪盈眶。

1111
00:54:15.240 --> 00:54:16.520
It was so sweet.
太暖心了。

1112
00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:17.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1113
00:54:17.700 --> 00:54:24.240
Guys, we didn't go to the character of Kevin very often for a heartfelt moment on the show.
伙计们，我们在剧中很少让凯文这个角色展现走心的时刻。

1114
00:54:24.540 --> 00:54:30.020
And it's a shame because Brian Baumgartner is a fantastic actor.
这很可惜，因为布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳是一位出色的演员。

1115
00:54:30.320 --> 00:54:30.500
Yeah.
没错。

1116
00:54:30.500 --> 00:54:33.060
And you can see that in this talking head.
你可以在这段采访中看出来。

1117
00:54:33.420 --> 00:54:33.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1118
00:54:34.060 --> 00:54:37.360
I was excited to get to see this performance from him.
我很高兴能看到他这样的表演。

1119
00:54:37.820 --> 00:54:38.660
Great job, Bea.
干得好，小布。

1120
00:54:39.300 --> 00:54:39.720
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1121
00:54:39.840 --> 00:54:42.880
Michael has come back from his date and he's very angry.
迈克尔约会回来了，他非常生气。

1122
00:54:43.240 --> 00:54:43.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1123
00:54:44.160 --> 00:54:45.680
He gives a big speech.
他发表了一大通演说。

1124
00:54:46.220 --> 00:54:48.920
Angela, here are the things that he's a man of.
安吉拉，以下是他所具备的特质。

1125
00:54:49.600 --> 00:54:50.120
Intensity.
激情。

1126
00:54:50.400 --> 00:54:50.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1127
00:54:51.020 --> 00:54:51.460
Cool.
酷。

1128
00:54:51.940 --> 00:54:52.460
Youth.
青春。

1129
00:54:52.660 --> 00:54:53.700
And passionately.
还有热情地。

1130
00:54:54.440 --> 00:54:56.000
He's a man of passionately.
他是一个热情地的人。

1131
00:54:56.620 --> 00:54:59.120
He's a man of youth and passionately.
他是一个青春且热情地的人。

1132
00:54:59.800 --> 00:55:05.820
Well, at 15 minutes, 10 seconds, you might notice I'm writing on the top of my desk.
嗯，在15分10秒的时候，你们可能会注意到我在桌面上写字。

1133
00:55:05.960 --> 00:55:10.980
I have several papers on this very little thin lip of the top of my desk.
我的办公桌边缘很窄，上面放了好几张纸。

1134
00:55:11.440 --> 00:55:17.760
I had to do that for camera because when I was staging my writing on the actual desk,
我必须为了拍摄这么做，因为如果我在桌面上正常写字的话，

1135
00:55:17.920 --> 00:55:20.020
they couldn't see my face when Michael entered.
迈克尔进来时他们就拍不到我的脸了。

1136
00:55:20.300 --> 00:55:25.940
I have to imagine that was a tough reach and very awkward because you're leaning over your desk
我能想象那一定很难够到，而且非常别扭，因为你得趴在桌子上

1137
00:55:25.940 --> 00:55:28.080
to write on a tiny ledge.
在那个小边沿上写字。

1138
00:55:28.080 --> 00:55:29.820
Well, I'll tell you something.
嗯，我告诉你一件事。

1139
00:55:30.020 --> 00:55:33.360
Pam's desk was very narrow in general.
帕姆的桌子总体来说非常窄。

1140
00:55:33.620 --> 00:55:36.440
I couldn't fit more than a keyboard on it.
除了键盘我什么都放不下。

1141
00:55:36.580 --> 00:55:42.840
In order to write on Pam's actual desk, which was made very thin, I think, for production,
为了在帕姆真正的桌子上写字——我觉得那桌子是为了拍摄做得特别窄——

1142
00:55:43.560 --> 00:55:44.860
it was always awkward.
总是很别扭。

1143
00:55:45.140 --> 00:55:45.520
Always.
一直都很别扭。

1144
00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:46.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1145
00:55:46.580 --> 00:55:49.860
So I've perched up on that little ledge, which was also awkward.
所以我只能在那小边沿上凑合，那也很别扭。

1146
00:55:50.440 --> 00:55:55.160
In this scene, Jenna, it seems like Jim and Pam are just kind of teasing each other.
珍娜，在这一幕里，吉姆和帕姆看起来像是在互相调侃。

1147
00:55:55.340 --> 00:55:58.620
Like, he's like, what were you thinking setting Michael up with your landlord?
就像他在说，你撮合迈克尔和你房东的时候在想什么呢？

1148
00:55:58.920 --> 00:56:00.200
Now you have to move out.
现在你得搬家了。

1149
00:56:00.400 --> 00:56:01.220
That went horribly.
那次约会简直糟透了。

1150
00:56:01.680 --> 00:56:02.900
And they're kind of joking.
他们当时是在开玩笑。

1151
00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:05.240
And she's like, maybe I should move in with my boyfriend.
她说，也许我该搬去和男朋友同居。

1152
00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:08.100
And then Pam has a moment of vulnerability.
然后帕姆流露出了脆弱的一面。

1153
00:56:08.100 --> 00:56:13.240
And you see it in your face, Jenna, where you're going to be an advocate for yourself.
珍娜，从你的表情就能看出来，你准备要为自己争取了。

1154
00:56:13.440 --> 00:56:15.000
This is something you've been working on.
这是你一直在努力的事情。

1155
00:56:15.440 --> 00:56:16.600
And she says, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

1156
00:56:16.660 --> 00:56:19.860
I'm only going to move in with my boyfriend if I'm engaged.
除非订婚，否则我不会搬去和男朋友同居。

1157
00:56:20.320 --> 00:56:20.700
Yeah.
没错。

1158
00:56:21.060 --> 00:56:22.620
And Jim doesn't miss a beat.
吉姆反应极快。

1159
00:56:22.800 --> 00:56:23.960
He's like, oh, it's coming.
他说，哦，快了。

1160
00:56:24.300 --> 00:56:25.020
Of course.
当然。

1161
00:56:25.020 --> 00:56:28.960
And then Pam just kind of keeps joking along.
然后帕姆就顺着他的话开玩笑。

1162
00:56:29.140 --> 00:56:30.920
And Jenna, I was like, does Pam?
珍娜，我当时在想，帕姆知道吗？

1163
00:56:31.120 --> 00:56:35.040
I mean, in the moment, I was positive that Jim was serious.
我是说，在那一刻，我确信吉姆是认真的。

1164
00:56:35.380 --> 00:56:36.560
Does Pam know?
帕姆知道吗？

1165
00:56:36.920 --> 00:56:38.660
Does Pam know he's doing a bit?
帕姆知道他在演戏吗？

1166
00:56:38.820 --> 00:56:40.900
Does it hit her that he's not?
她意识到他其实没在开玩笑吗？

1167
00:56:41.740 --> 00:56:50.260
I think this maybe in my backstory was kind of one of the first times that this idea of
我觉得这可能是我设定的背景故事里，第一次出现关于

1168
00:56:50.260 --> 00:56:53.440
them getting engaged or married has really come up.
他们订婚或结婚的想法。

1169
00:56:54.260 --> 00:57:00.460
And that was a reason why I chose to kind of hesitate as well when Pam says, oh, I'm not
这也是为什么当帕姆说“哦，除非订婚，否则我不会

1170
00:57:00.460 --> 00:57:06.280
going to move in with anyone until I'm engaged, is because this idea of being engaged, it's
和任何人同居”时，我会犹豫的原因，因为“订婚”这个念头，

1171
00:57:06.280 --> 00:57:10.220
not something that I thought they had talked about a lot yet.
我觉得他们还没怎么讨论过。

1172
00:57:10.520 --> 00:57:12.520
No, and that's how it reads.
没错，看起来确实是这样。

1173
00:57:12.520 --> 00:57:17.760
As an audience, I loved it because this is how real life stuff comes up.
作为观众，我很喜欢这一点，因为现实生活中的事情就是这样发生的。

1174
00:57:17.900 --> 00:57:21.100
Sometimes it just seeps in to like a mundane conversation.
有时它只是悄悄渗入一段平凡的对话中。

1175
00:57:21.100 --> 00:57:23.160
And then you're like, oh, crap, we're here now.
然后你会突然意识到，糟了，我们聊到这儿了。

1176
00:57:23.440 --> 00:57:23.800
OK.
好的。

1177
00:57:24.380 --> 00:57:24.720
Yes.
是的。

1178
00:57:24.980 --> 00:57:29.180
And so I think Pam isn't totally sure what to do with this conversation.
所以我认为帕姆并不完全确定该如何应对这段对话。

1179
00:57:29.400 --> 00:57:30.420
Was it a bit?
他是在演戏吗？

1180
00:57:30.580 --> 00:57:31.460
Is he being serious?
他是认真的吗？

1181
00:57:31.860 --> 00:57:38.020
Now, he has a talking head for the audience where he says, oh, I'm not kidding.
现在，他对着镜头说，哦，我没开玩笑。

1182
00:57:38.320 --> 00:57:43.400
I got this a week after we started dating and he shows an engagement ring.
我们开始约会一周后我就买了，然后他展示了一枚订婚戒指。

1183
00:57:43.920 --> 00:57:44.920
And I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1184
00:57:45.160 --> 00:57:47.160
Does he carry it to work with him every day?
他每天都随身带着戒指去上班吗？

1185
00:57:47.500 --> 00:57:48.460
I don't know.
我不知道。

1186
00:57:48.600 --> 00:57:49.780
Does it live in his pocket?
它一直放在他口袋里吗？

1187
00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:52.280
Is he too worried to leave it at his apartment?
他是不是太担心把它留在公寓里了？

1188
00:57:52.580 --> 00:57:55.360
Like, he has it ready to go.
就像是，他随时准备着。

1189
00:57:56.240 --> 00:58:02.320
We had a fan question from Abigail B who said, is the ring Jim shows the camera the ring he
我们收到了一位粉丝Abigail B的提问，她说，吉姆展示给镜头看的那枚戒指，

1190
00:58:02.320 --> 00:58:06.440
proposes with later and the one that Pam wears for the rest of the show?
是他后来求婚时用的那枚，也是帕姆在剧集余下部分一直戴着的那枚吗？

1191
00:58:06.440 --> 00:58:08.780
So I think it is.
我觉得是的。

1192
00:58:09.280 --> 00:58:10.980
I think that it is.
我想应该是的。

1193
00:58:11.120 --> 00:58:16.620
I remember Phil Shea coming up to me and presenting me with a tray of rings.
我记得菲尔·谢伊走过来，递给我一托盘的戒指。

1194
00:58:16.620 --> 00:58:23.720
And he and I had a very long conversation about what kind of ring would Jim buy Pam?
我和他进行了很长一段时间的讨论，关于吉姆会给帕姆买什么样的戒指？

1195
00:58:24.260 --> 00:58:26.660
Like, Jim's going to hit it out of the park for Pam.
毕竟，吉姆一定会为帕姆选到最完美的戒指。

1196
00:58:26.840 --> 00:58:30.000
Remember, Pam was always a little disappointed in her ring from Roy.
别忘了，帕姆一直对罗伊送她的那枚戒指有点失望。

1197
00:58:30.140 --> 00:58:31.160
That was my backstory.
那是我的背景设定。

1198
00:58:31.500 --> 00:58:32.100
The cluster.
那枚碎钻拼成的戒指。

1199
00:58:32.540 --> 00:58:32.940
Yes.
没错。

1200
00:58:33.320 --> 00:58:38.040
And so Phil was like, what would make Pam's heart sing?
所以菲尔当时问，什么样的戒指会让帕姆心动不已？

1201
00:58:38.720 --> 00:58:40.640
And I remember picking that ring.
我还记得当时选那枚戒指的情景。

1202
00:58:41.480 --> 00:58:43.820
So, yeah, I think it is that ring.
所以，没错，我觉得就是那枚戒指。

1203
00:58:43.820 --> 00:58:48.780
So, pretty bold move, Jim, to buy it the first week you guys started dating.
吉姆，你们刚开始约会的第一周就买戒指，这招挺大胆的啊。

1204
00:58:49.040 --> 00:58:49.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1205
00:58:49.520 --> 00:58:51.680
But I guess he knew he loved her for a long time.
但我猜他早就知道自己爱她很久了。

1206
00:58:52.100 --> 00:58:52.300
Yeah.
没错。

1207
00:58:52.540 --> 00:58:56.380
Well, guys, here's the scene that's in Michael's office that I love.
好了，各位，接下来是迈克办公室里的一场戏，我特别喜欢。

1208
00:58:56.500 --> 00:58:57.740
It's shot a little differently.
它的拍摄手法有点不同。

1209
00:58:57.960 --> 00:58:59.020
This was Jeff Blitz.
那是杰夫·布里茨拍的。

1210
00:58:59.300 --> 00:59:04.960
You know, there's always so many of the same scenes in the same places because we only had
你知道，因为我们只有一个摄影棚，所以很多戏总是在同样的地方拍摄，

1211
00:59:04.960 --> 00:59:05.640
one set.
场景很有限。

1212
00:59:05.780 --> 00:59:09.060
And every once in a while, a director would find a fun way to shoot.
偶尔会有导演想出有趣的拍摄方式。

1213
00:59:09.400 --> 00:59:13.700
And Jeff Blitz had this idea for this scene between Michael and Dwight that he would
杰夫·布里茨对迈克和德怀特之间的这场戏有个想法，他打算

1214
00:59:13.700 --> 00:59:21.840
just lower the camera a little and shoot at an angle and slowly push in as Dwight convinces
把摄像机放低一点，以一个角度拍摄，然后缓慢推进，当时德怀特正在说服

1215
00:59:21.840 --> 00:59:24.640
Michael that what he needs is closure.
迈克，说他需要的是了结。

1216
00:59:25.060 --> 00:59:31.340
And when I watched the scene, there was a brief moment that I thought he meant with Jan.
当我看到这场戏时，有一瞬间我以为他指的是简。

1217
00:59:31.600 --> 00:59:31.960
Same.
我也是。

1218
00:59:32.120 --> 00:59:33.980
He needs closure with Jan.
他需要和简做个了结。

1219
00:59:34.200 --> 00:59:35.140
But no.
但并不是。

1220
00:59:35.420 --> 00:59:35.720
No.
不是。

1221
00:59:35.860 --> 00:59:37.100
It's with the chair model.
是和那位椅子模特。

1222
00:59:37.520 --> 00:59:39.440
So they head to the cemetery.
于是他们去了墓地。

1223
00:59:39.740 --> 00:59:41.460
Of a woman he's never met.
去祭奠一个他从未谋面的女人。

1224
00:59:41.780 --> 00:59:42.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1225
00:59:42.140 --> 00:59:43.380
That's right.
没错。

1226
00:59:43.580 --> 00:59:52.820
And they are going to launch into a tribute to her by singing a version of American Pie.
他们准备通过演唱《美国派》的改编版来向她致敬。

1227
00:59:53.480 --> 00:59:53.980
Bye.
再见。

1228
00:59:54.360 --> 00:59:56.580
Bye, Miss Chair Model Lady.
再见，椅子模特小姐。

1229
00:59:57.160 --> 01:00:01.210
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1230
01:00:01.390 --> 01:00:05.310
So, you know, the writers actually had a hard time getting a song cleared for this.
所以，你知道，编剧们其实很难为这一段搞定歌曲版权。

1231
01:00:05.770 --> 01:00:06.390
Shocker.
真让人吃惊。

1232
01:00:06.390 --> 01:00:13.290
The first song they were going to parody was Elton John's Candle in the Wind, but they could
他们原本打算恶搞的第一首歌是埃尔顿·约翰的《风中之烛》，但他们没能

1233
01:00:13.290 --> 01:00:19.630
not get the rights because, here's an interesting bit of trivia, he had given permission for
拿到版权，因为这里有个有趣的冷知识，他曾授权过

1234
01:00:19.630 --> 01:00:23.350
the song to be parodied on 30 Rock, and he did not care for the results.
这首歌在《我为喜剧狂》中被恶搞，但他对结果很不满意。

1235
01:00:23.350 --> 01:00:26.670
So he said no more parodies of Candle in the Wind.
所以他说以后不再允许恶搞《风中之烛》了。

1236
01:00:26.930 --> 01:00:27.230
No.
不会吧。

1237
01:00:27.650 --> 01:00:27.950
Okay.
好吧。

1238
01:00:27.950 --> 01:00:31.930
They also wrote parodies of Legs by ZZ Top.
他们还写了ZZ Top乐队《美腿》的恶搞版。

1239
01:00:32.350 --> 01:00:34.010
She's got legs.
她有一双美腿。

1240
01:00:34.230 --> 01:00:37.050
How is that a song you sing at a gravesite?
那怎么能是在墓地唱的歌呢？

1241
01:00:37.230 --> 01:00:40.470
She was a chair model, and you really see her legs in the picture.
因为她是椅子模特，而且照片里确实能看到她的腿。

1242
01:00:40.850 --> 01:00:42.170
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1243
01:00:42.290 --> 01:00:42.510
Okay.
好吧。

1244
01:00:43.010 --> 01:00:46.030
And then also Ruby Tuesday by the Rolling Stones.
还有滚石乐队的《红宝石星期二》。

1245
01:00:46.370 --> 01:00:48.030
Oh, I love Ruby Tuesday.
哦，我喜欢《红宝石星期二》。

1246
01:00:48.330 --> 01:00:53.630
But the song that got cleared was American Pie, and I'm so glad it did because I really love
但最终获批的是《美国派》，我很高兴是这首，因为我真的很喜欢

1247
01:00:53.630 --> 01:00:56.290
them in the dark singing.
他们在黑暗中唱歌的样子。

1248
01:00:57.150 --> 01:01:01.470
Well, we can't wrap up this episode without this adorable scene.
好了，我们不能在没有这场可爱戏份的情况下结束这一集。

1249
01:01:01.730 --> 01:01:08.610
Jenna, I literally wrote adorable and highlighted it between Jim and Pam as they're walking to
珍娜，我特意写了“可爱”并加了高亮，就是吉姆和帕姆走去

1250
01:01:08.610 --> 01:01:12.230
the satellite parking lot, and the sun is setting.
卫星停车场，夕阳西下的那一幕。

1251
01:01:12.450 --> 01:01:14.610
You guys both look like angels.
你们俩看起来都像天使一样。

1252
01:01:15.030 --> 01:01:17.350
You both look so flippin' adorable.
你们俩看起来真是可爱极了。

1253
01:01:17.770 --> 01:01:20.830
Well, I remember we had to wait in our trailer for that light.
我记得当时我们为了等那束光，不得不待在拖车里。

1254
01:01:21.030 --> 01:01:22.790
That's called the magic hour.
那叫魔幻时刻。

1255
01:01:22.950 --> 01:01:23.370
Yeah.
没错。

1256
01:01:23.370 --> 01:01:28.630
In the biz, and there's this little 45 minutes when the sun is truly magical.
在业内，太阳落山前有那短短45分钟，光线真的非常神奇。

1257
01:01:29.310 --> 01:01:31.630
Everybody, take your photos at magic hour.
大家都要在魔幻时刻拍照。

1258
01:01:31.790 --> 01:01:32.950
It's when you look the beSt.
那是你看起来最美的时候。

1259
01:01:33.110 --> 01:01:33.590
That's right.
说得对。

1260
01:01:33.690 --> 01:01:37.030
If you're planning a wedding, plan for some, like, magic hour photos.
如果你在筹备婚礼，记得安排一些魔幻时刻的照片。

1261
01:01:37.490 --> 01:01:37.690
Yeah.
没错。

1262
01:01:37.990 --> 01:01:43.010
So, we waited for that moment, and we could only do a few takes because then we were
所以我们一直在等那个瞬间，而且我们只能拍几次，因为之后就

1263
01:01:43.010 --> 01:01:43.870
going to lose the light.
没光了。

1264
01:01:44.170 --> 01:01:45.890
He drops to one knee.
他单膝跪下了。

1265
01:01:46.370 --> 01:01:46.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1266
01:01:47.210 --> 01:01:52.470
Well, I'll tell you, this moment was promo'd like crazy.
我跟你说，这一幕的宣传力度简直疯狂。

1267
01:01:52.470 --> 01:01:53.230
Crazy.
疯狂。

1268
01:01:53.230 --> 01:01:53.990
Like, crazy.
简直疯狂。

1269
01:01:54.350 --> 01:01:55.990
I bet they blasted it out.
我敢说他们肯定大肆宣传了一番。

1270
01:01:56.250 --> 01:01:56.770
Yeah.
没错。

1271
01:01:57.070 --> 01:02:02.070
Well, you know, we talked about how season four was interrupted by the writer's strike.
你知道的，我们聊过第四季是如何被编剧罢工打断的。

1272
01:02:02.070 --> 01:02:09.370
The writers originally had this very, very big storyline for Jim and Pam that I think involved
编剧们原本为吉姆和帕姆构思了一条非常非常宏大的故事线，我想是关于

1273
01:02:09.370 --> 01:02:11.930
them moving in together, if I'm correct.
他们搬到一起住，如果我没记错的话。

1274
01:02:11.930 --> 01:02:18.250
And instead, because we lost a bunch of episodes, they were like, you know what?
结果因为少拍了好几集，他们就想，不如这样吧？

1275
01:02:18.250 --> 01:02:20.990
We should skip that, and they should just get engaged.
我们跳过那段，直接让他们订婚。

1276
01:02:21.010 --> 01:02:25.810
Or we should just skip to the part where we're thinking they might get engaged any minute.
或者直接跳到那种大家觉得他们随时可能订婚的阶段。

1277
01:02:26.090 --> 01:02:29.690
And so, that was where this part of the story came from.
所以，这就是这段剧情的由来。

1278
01:02:30.350 --> 01:02:30.930
I like it.
我喜欢这个安排。

1279
01:02:31.070 --> 01:02:33.070
I like that Pam still had her own place.
我喜欢帕姆当时还有自己的住处。

1280
01:02:33.390 --> 01:02:33.730
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1281
01:02:33.730 --> 01:02:38.630
I like all of that storyline for her, because you sort of feel like Pam lived with Roy for
我喜欢她那条故事线的所有内容，因为你会觉得帕姆之前和罗伊一起住了

1282
01:02:38.630 --> 01:02:39.670
a long time.
很长一段时间。

1283
01:02:40.070 --> 01:02:43.490
And then she finally carved out her own space in the world.
然后她终于在世界上开辟出了属于自己的空间。

1284
01:02:43.590 --> 01:02:46.030
And I really liked that choice.
我真的很喜欢这个选择。

1285
01:02:46.290 --> 01:02:50.250
Well, your reaction when you realize that Jim is faking is so great.
你意识到吉姆是在假装时的反应真是太棒了。

1286
01:02:50.370 --> 01:02:51.210
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1287
01:02:51.350 --> 01:02:52.250
You're like, I hate you.
你当时就像是说，我讨厌你。

1288
01:02:52.410 --> 01:02:53.290
And he's like, what?
然后他说，怎么了？

1289
01:02:53.490 --> 01:02:54.590
It's really cute.
真的很可爱。

1290
01:02:55.170 --> 01:02:55.410
Yeah.
没错。

1291
01:02:55.870 --> 01:02:57.530
I have some bad news.
我有个坏消息。

1292
01:02:58.150 --> 01:02:58.370
What?
什么？

1293
01:02:58.770 --> 01:03:02.030
I mean, spoiler alert, Pam's going to need to go to art school.
我是说，剧透预警，帕姆要去上艺术学校了。

1294
01:03:02.390 --> 01:03:03.950
We're going to frustrate you.
我们要让你感到沮丧了。

1295
01:03:04.190 --> 01:03:04.770
I know.
我知道。

1296
01:03:05.050 --> 01:03:08.690
This proposal's going to take a little while, but we're planting the seeds.
这次求婚还要等上一阵子，但我们正在埋下伏笔。

1297
01:03:08.930 --> 01:03:11.770
They have to pull you guys apart to put you back together.
他们必须先让你们分开，才能再让你们重聚。

1298
01:03:11.970 --> 01:03:12.870
It makes me crazy.
这让我抓狂。

1299
01:03:13.290 --> 01:03:14.250
I know.
我知道。

1300
01:03:14.690 --> 01:03:17.710
Well, guys, that is chair model.
好了，伙计们，这就是《椅子模特》那一集。

1301
01:03:18.270 --> 01:03:20.110
Next up is night out.
接下来是“夜生活”那一集。

1302
01:03:20.850 --> 01:03:24.150
I'm really enjoying season four, Angela, I have to say.
安吉拉，我不得不说，我真的很喜欢第四季。

1303
01:03:24.150 --> 01:03:25.350
Me too.
我也是。

1304
01:03:25.750 --> 01:03:26.810
So fun.
太有趣了。

1305
01:03:27.030 --> 01:03:31.530
And for all of you chair models out there, just know your work is not in vain.
对于所有那些椅子模特们，要知道你们的工作并非徒劳。

1306
01:03:31.850 --> 01:03:35.050
You might be inspiring others to find true love.
你们或许正在激励他人寻找真爱。

1307
01:03:35.270 --> 01:03:42.950
And Paul, thank you so much for sending in these audio clips and being so quick to respond when
还有保罗，非常感谢你发来这些音频片段，并且在我给你发短信时

1308
01:03:42.950 --> 01:03:43.730
I texted you.
回复得那么快。

1309
01:03:43.910 --> 01:03:45.530
You are just such a delight.
你真是太可爱了。

1310
01:03:45.750 --> 01:03:47.110
And I adore you.
我非常喜欢你。

1311
01:03:47.310 --> 01:03:48.750
And these made our day, Jenna.
这些让我们的这一天都变得美好了，珍娜。

